Auto-Scaffold on Intent. Add it into vaca

### 1. The Intent Map (`vaca/config/intent_scaffolds.json`)
This file defines what triggers auto-scaffold. It’s declarative so you can expand it later without touching Python logic.

```json
{
  "scaffolds": [
    {
      "id": "node-express-api",
      "triggers": ["express server", "rest api node", "backend node"],
      "files": {
        "/server.js": "// Auto-scaffolded by VACA\nconst express = require('express');\nconst app = express();\napp.use(express.json());\napp.get('/', (req, res) => res.send({ status: 'ok', message: 'VACA scaffold active' }));\napp.listen(3000, () => console.log('Server running on port 3000'));\n",
        "/package.json": "{ \"name\": \"vaca-scaffold\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\", \"dependencies\": { \"express\": \"^4.18.2\" } }\n",
        "/README.md": "# VACA Auto-Scaffold\nGenerated by intent detection: node-express-api\n"
      },
      "post_message": "I’ve scaffolded your Express API structure in `data/chat-files/`. The server file, package.json, and README are ready. Want me to add a specific route next?"
    },
    {
      "id": "python-fastapi",
      "triggers": ["fastapi app", "python api backend"],
      "files": {
        "/main.py": "# Auto-scaffolded by VACA\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\napp = FastAPI()\n@app.get('/')\ndef read_root(): return {'status': 'ok', 'scaffold': True}\n",
        "/requirements.txt": "fastapi==0.104.1\nuvicorn[standard]==0.23.2\n"
      },
      "post_message": "FastAPI scaffold ready in `data/chat-files/`. Main.py and requirements.txt are created. Shall I add a Pydantic model or middleware?"
    }
  ]
}
```

